        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Hydrated lanthanum halide, LH2 [1-(2-hydroxyphenyl)-3-(2-thienyl)-1,3-propanedione], and triethylamine were reacted in methanol in a 1:2:4 ratio, affording a yellow precipitate. The hexanuclear cluster encapsulates a μ6-CO3^2− ion introduced by spontaneous fixation of atmospheric CO2 in the basic medium; no carbonate reagent was added. Direct attempts using carbonate reagents or crystallization in a closed system failed to give diffraction-quality crystals of 1–3.",
